\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Yes. I did a fairly deep pass across UDS\'92s current corporate structure, Denave\'92s product footprint, the major consent-management platforms, current DPDP legislation/rules, mobile-platform requirements, and some developer/community feedback.\
One terminology correction first: I\'92m assuming you mean 
\f1\b Updater Services Limited (UDS)
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b Denave India Private Limited
\f0\b0 . UDS is the parent/group, and Denave is the sales-enablement company you referred to. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uds.in/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 UDS}})\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 My conclusion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Do not build a \'93consent banner product.\'94
\f0\b0 \
For UDS, I would build a 
\f1\b Group Privacy & Consent Control Plane
\f0\b0 : a centralized service that manages consent, preferences, lawful-purpose configuration, privacy notices, vendor permissions, identity linking, audit evidence and enforcement across every UDS company, product, website, mobile application and backend system.\
The critical design principle should be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Centralized policy and evidence, distributed enforcement.
\f0\b0 \
That is the architecture that gives you the potential to be significantly better than a conventional CMP such as OneTrust/Usercentrics/Ketch or an India-focused DPDP consent product.\
UDS's current group footprint makes this unusually important. Its FY2026 consolidated structure includes UDS itself plus Wynwy, Global Flight Handling and five step-down entities, Fusion Foods, Avon, Matrix, Washroom Hygiene Concepts, UDS Foundation, Denave and its five international subsidiaries, and Athena BPO with a step-down subsidiary.\
And Denave alone operates across 
\f1\b 5 continents, 50+ countries and 500+ cities
\f0\b0 , with operations in India, Singapore, Malaysia, South Korea and the UK. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denave.com/en-in/about-us/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 https://www.denave.com}})\
So your problem is fundamentally different from:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93Put a cookie banner on our website.\'94\
It is closer to:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93How does one person\'92s privacy decision propagate correctly across a group containing dozens of applications and very different technology stacks?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

